Package: sparsepca
Type: Package
Title: Sparse Principal Component Analysis
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("N. Benjamin", "Erichson", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "erichson@icsi.berkeley.edu"),
    person("Peng", "Zheng", role = "aut"),
    person("Sasha", "Aravkin", role = "aut"),
    person("Maria", "Sans-Fuentes", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Reported the robust objective error"))
Description: Fits principal components with sparse loading vectors for
    interpretable dimension reduction. Variable projection combines an
    orthogonal reconstruction factor with elastic net or cardinality
    regularization of the loadings. Deterministic, randomized, and robust
    algorithms support exploratory analysis of high-dimensional data;
    the randomized algorithm also supports sparse input matrices through
    implicit centering and scaling. A robust formulation separates
    entrywise outliers from the low-rank reconstruction. Regularization
    paths reuse matrix factorizations, and prediction applies the fitted
    transformation to new observations. The methods are described in
    Erichson et al. (2020) <doi:10.1137/18M1211350>.
